<h2>Segment 236 &mdash; essence and mistaken perception</h2>
<div class="pair">
<div class="tib"><div class="lab">TIBETAN (WYLIE)</div>
<span class="u" data-d="1" data-l="s236S"><span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s236w1">rang gi</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s236w2">ngo bo nyid</span> <span class="u case" data-d="6" data-l="s236p1">kyis</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s236w3">grub</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s236w4">na</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s236w5">gnas lugs</span> su <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s236w6">grub</span> par &#x27;gyur la, de&#x27;i tshe <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s236w7">&#x27;khrul pa</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s236w8">log pa</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s236w9">na</span> gsal du &#x27;gro dgos kyi, <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s236w10">ldog</span> par <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s236w11">mi</span> &#x27;gyur ro, , zhes pa&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s236w12">don</span> no</span>
</div>
<div class="eng"><div class="lab">GESHE MICHAEL'S ENGLISH (VERBATIM)</div>
<span class="u" data-d="1" data-l="s236S">The <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s236w12">meaning</span> of the lines is as follows. <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s236w4">If</span> things <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s236w3">existed</span> <span class="u case" data-d="6" data-l="s236p1">in</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s236w1">their</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s236w2">very essence</span>, then they would <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s236w6">exist</span> as some <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s236w5">independent reality</span>. If this were so, then <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s236w9">when</span> you finally <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s236w8">stopped</span> your <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s236w7">mistaken states of mind</span>, they would <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s236w11">never</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s236w10">disappear</span>, although they should have.</span>
</div>
</div>
<div class="note"><b>AI NOTE</b> &mdash; PROVISIONAL machine alignment reconciled by Codex from independent Tibetan-first and English-first proposals; no human semantic acceptance. rang gi licenses their and kyis the contextual means/essence expression in. The first grub owns existed and the second grub owns the separate whole word exist. gnas lugs/independent reality and ngo bo nyid/very essence are glossary attestations. 'khrul pa is a nominal error/delusion here, rendered contextually as the whole mistaken states of mind; its HGM entry attests mistaken and delusion, not that exact full phrase. Initial na owns If and later na owns when. Supplied things, they, you, your, finally and auxiliary wording stay unpaired. The temporal de'i tshe/If this were so recast and the expanded introductory formula are omitted; don retains meaning. ldog owns disappear and mi owns never. gsal du 'gro dgos kyi and although they should have remain unresolved and omitted, not nulled: the glossary's HGM25759 explicitly attests gsal du 'gro/disappear at HTG2016 tier, while ILL's full corresponding passage uses brought-to-light wording. The proposed categorical English erratum is refuted for insufficient certainty given this actual attestation and the possible argument-level elliptical recast; neither interpretation is substituted into the source. All source text remains verbatim.</div>
